    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** standing out as the clear offensive engine. His 80.29 score is boosted by a favorable matchup against Lorenzen and a move to the two-hole, providing optimal leverage for both his power and the high-value stolen base potential we prioritize. Complementing him are **Brice Turang** (74.07) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (69.05), both of whom capitalize on soft matchups against Sasaki and Giolito, respectively. **Brice Turang** in particular benefits from a massive 19% SP skill adjustment, making him our most efficient play outside of **Corbin Carroll**. Meanwhile, **James Wood** remains a high-floor start thanks to his elite .380 xwOBA and top-of-the-order protection, which should help mitigate the general volatility of his profile.\n\nStrategic considerations for today revolve around minimizing risk against top-tier arms while squeezing value from platoon advantages. **Travis Bazzana** is the most precarious start of the day; his 42.35 score is heavily impacted by a wind-in factor and a brutal matchup against the elite Wheeler (2.87 xERA). While **Kyle Karros** was our most viable alternative on the bench (45.78), his position at the bottom of the order and lower base projection relegated him to the pine. We are also wary of **Vinnie Pasquantino**\u2019s matchup against Kirby; despite a strong platoon adjustment (+14%), the high-skill nature of the opposing pitcher makes this a sub-60 projection that we are monitoring closely. **Jose Caballero** remains sidelined due to a postponement, reinforcing our focus on those active in today\u2019s favorable weather conditions.",
